"""All attacks use the held staff; support legs never become attack weapons."""
STYLE='''PIXEL-ART fighting-game animation sheet. Preserve this character's exact face, eyes, hair/spikes, colors, clothing and body proportions. TWO arms and TWO legs, all attached and fully visible. A LARGE RED-AND-GOLD STAFF about as tall as the actor, with a clearly curled/spiral top, is held securely in one or both hands in EVERY pose. This is a proper full-length staff, not a tiny wand. Every melee action hits with the STAFF: thrust, overhead swing, low sweep and airborne staff strike. Legs only support or tuck during jumps; do not kick as the attack. Coherent wrists and two-handed grips. Entire staff fits wholly inside each cell with generous empty margins. Solid pure magenta #ff00ff background, crisp stepped pixels, dark outlines, compact shading, no labels, grid lines, floating effects or detached props. Exactly one complete actor per cell.'''
CORE='''Exactly 32 complete figures, regular FOUR columns by EIGHT rows. Four figures in every row.
Row 1: staff guard; subtle breathing staff guard; near guarded step; passing step.
Row 2: far guarded step; far passing step; low staff-guarded dash; jump anticipation.
Row 3: rising jump with staff close; falling jump with staff close; crouched landing; draw staff back to thrust.
Row 4: straight STAFF THRUST to RIGHT; retract staff; coil staff low for rising swing; UPWARD STAFF SWING.
Row 5: chamber overhead staff swing; staff halfway through overhead swing; full STAFF IMPACT toward RIGHT, feet planted; retract after swing.
Row 6: LOW STAFF SWEEP at knee height to RIGHT, no kick; sweep recovery; airborne STAFF STRIKE chamber, knees tucked; airborne STAFF STRIKE to RIGHT, no kick.
Row 7: hit recoil retaining staff; high staff guard; hook staff forward to catch; staff-assisted hold, no opponent.
Row 8: staff lever throw follow-through, no opponent; staff power charge; staff channel release to RIGHT, no projectile; powerful two-handed STAFF SPECIAL impact.'''
WALK='''Exactly EIGHT separate figures in FOUR columns and TWO rows. Guarded footwork cycle with staff held securely in BOTH hands: near foot plants; weight transfers over near sole; far knee passes under low hips; far foot reaches; far foot plants; weight transfers over far sole; near knee passes; near foot reaches. Staff stays about body-height and attached to hands in every drawing. Same face and body size throughout. Feet alternate readable ground support without sliding hips. No running or weapons floating apart.'''
EVENTS='''Exactly 32 complete figures, regular FOUR columns by EIGHT rows. Four figures in every row.
Row 1 INTRO: guarded staff; secure small staff twirl; confident staff salute; settle staff guard.
Row 2 SPECIAL A: staff back coil; strong two-handed windup; straight STAFF THRUST to RIGHT; retract staff.
Row 3 SPECIAL B: overhead STAFF STRIKE; staff retract cover; emphatic finishing STAFF SWING to RIGHT; staff guard recovery.
Row 4 CAST: staff close to chest; staff tip raised to aim; staff points forward to channel energy, no projectile; return staff guard.
Row 5 RECOIL: chest recoil holding staff; head/torso lean; knees absorb; regain staff guard.
Row 6 DEFEAT: stagger; knees buckle; drop with staff in hand; roll onto side, whole staff visible and touching hand.
Row 7 FLOOR REST: side-lying, head LEFT feet RIGHT, staff safely beside body touching hand; settle lying; shoulder relaxes; entirely still lying.
Row 8 FINAL REST: same complete lying body and staff; relaxed lying body; hold floor rest; final still side-lying body with staff. Never stand or kneel in the final eight frames.'''
